WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 10.9 · Legal, Compliance, Policies & Risk
Writing usable procedures

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A good procedure lets someone new do a real task the same way, safely.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Set trigger, roles, numbered steps, records and exceptions.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Test it with someone who did not write it.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Base emergency and safeguarding steps on local expert advice.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Riverside Repair Hub (Hybrid · charity with a trading company, United Kingdom)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Riverside: no electrical sold until tested, labelled and recorded; a failed item is tagged 'do not sell' and kept apart.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You write one priority procedure and plan its test.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
